happen|occur|VERB|take place|To take place or occur.|xảy ra|The power cut happened just before the concert began.|Sự cố mất điện xảy ra ngay trước khi buổi hòa nhạc bắt đầu.|Intransitive; what happened asks about an event, while happen to someone names who experiences it.|0
happen|by-chance|VERB|do something by chance|To do or be something by chance rather than because it was arranged.|tình cờ|I happened to meet our old neighbour at the station.|Tôi tình cờ gặp người hàng xóm cũ ở nhà ga.|Happen to plus an infinitive expresses chance; the infinitive need not describe a harmful event.|1
memorable|worth-remembering|ADJECTIVE|likely to be remembered|Special or striking enough to be remembered for a long time.|đáng nhớ|The children gave a memorable performance at the village festival.|Bọn trẻ có một màn biểu diễn đáng nhớ tại lễ hội của làng.|Before a noun or after a linking verb; memorable can describe good or bad experiences.|0
prohibit|forbid|VERB|officially forbid an activity|To forbid an activity or prevent it through a rule or authority.|cấm; không cho phép|The gallery rules prohibit flash photography.|Nội quy phòng trưng bày cấm chụp ảnh có đèn flash.|Transitive prohibit an activity; prohibit someone from doing something names the person and forbidden action.|0
vegetarian|person-not-eating-meat|NOUN|person avoiding meat and fish|A person who does not eat meat or fish.|người ăn chay|The vegetarian in our group chose a bean dish.|Người ăn chay trong nhóm chúng tôi chọn một món đậu.|Countable; some vegetarians eat eggs or dairy products, unlike vegans. This record proposes the person noun.|-
wooded|having-trees|ADJECTIVE|covered with trees|Having many trees growing over an area.|có nhiều cây; phủ cây rừng|A wooded hillside sheltered the houses from the wind.|Một sườn đồi nhiều cây che chắn những ngôi nhà khỏi gió.|Usually before a place noun; wooded describes tree cover, while wooden describes material.|-
